I replaced roughly $350 a month of prospecting software with about 600 lines of dependency-free Python.

The FOSS Lead Engine pulls real businesses from open data, checks them against an ideal customer profile, writes a specific opening line and stages the outreach.

## Open data handles sourcing

No paid lead database sits underneath the pipeline.

The system gathers public records, normalises them and keeps the source path visible.

## Every score keeps its reason

Each prospect record includes the reason behind its score. The shortlist stays inspectable rather than hiding the decision inside a rank.

The scoring rule is easier to change when the target market changes.

## Outreach remains staged

The engine prepares research and opening context without becoming an unsupervised sender.

The operator reviews the shortlist and decides who receives a message.

## Ownership is the larger saving

Replacing roughly $350 a month of SaaS helped my operating cost.

Owning the data path, scoring logic and workflow removed the larger dependency.

Built by handlit.
